      *> DESIGN EXAMPLE - NOT COMPILED OR PRODUCTION READY.
      *> COBOL-shaped control flow, not a complete program.
      *> Every PERFORM is a PROJECT operation, not an IBM API.
      *> Mapping: I001 Reader; I002 Normalizer; I003 StateStore.
      *> Requirements: CAP-004..CAP-012, CAP-015..CAP-017.
      *> Tests: AT-003..AT-012, AT-017..AT-019.
      *> No direct CALL of IXGCONN/IXGBRWSE: implement a qualified wrapper.

       CAPTURE-ONE-RECORD.
           PERFORM READ-RAW-RECORD-USING-APPROVED-WRAPPER
           EVALUATE TRUE
               WHEN READ-TEMPORARILY-EMPTY
                   PERFORM WAIT-WITHOUT-CHANGING-RESUME
               WHEN READ-GAP-OR-AUTH-FAILURE
                   PERFORM STOP-AND-REPORT
               WHEN READ-COMPLETE
                   PERFORM NORMALIZE-AND-CHECK-BOUNDS
                   IF NOT NORMALIZATION-VALID
                       PERFORM STOP-AND-REPORT
                   ELSE
                       PERFORM APPLY-CAPTURE-RECORD
                   END-IF
               WHEN OTHER
                   PERFORM STOP-AND-REPORT
           END-EVALUATE.

       APPLY-CAPTURE-RECORD.
           *> This contract must perform ONE atomic backend commit:
           *> readerFence/predecessor CAS, source dedup, UOW fragments,
           *> undo/decision state, spool readiness and recoverable resume.
           *> Do not replace it with independent writes to two VSAM files.
           PERFORM STATESTORE-APPLY-ATOMICALLY
           EVALUATE TRUE
               WHEN STORE-COMMITTED
                   PERFORM REPORT-DURABLE-PROGRESS
               WHEN STORE-ALREADY-APPLIED-WITH-SAME-HASH
                   PERFORM REPORT-DURABLE-PROGRESS
               WHEN OTHER
                   *> Ambiguous commit: consult identity/hash on recovery.
                   *> Do not advance an independent cursor here.
                   PERFORM STOP-AND-REPORT
           END-EVALUATE.

      *> The StateStore implements the normative UOW state machine:
      *> CHANGE -> OPEN; COMMIT -> COMMIT_OBSERVED.
      *> FULL_BACKOUT -> BACKOUT_OBSERVED, not immediate terminal discard.
      *> Either observed state may absorb PROVEN pre-outcome late parts.
      *> Completeness + surviving changes -> READY for commit only.
      *> Completeness after full backout -> DISCARDED; never publish.
      *> Partial undo affects only qualified targets, not the whole UOW.
      *> In-doubt/unknown ordering -> HELD, never commit on timeout.
      *> Large UOW spill must be durable and integrity-checked.
      *> Pin source history still needed by open UOWs or other readers.
      *> Do not add SYNCPOINT to original business transactions.
